WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.230
Good morning John,
yes you got to record the

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.831
15th anniversary video of
vlogbrothers but I, and this

00:00:04.831 --> 00:00:08.730
is a weird coincidence, one day
later get to record the 2,000th

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.700
vlogbrothers video on this
channel.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.700
And I woke up yesterday

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.140
to a massive dump of snow
which meant that Orin’s school was canceled 

00:00:15.408 --> 00:00:18.520
So all of my normal plans
went right out the window.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.690
So what do you get?

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.420
You get our
2000th video.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.699
A compilation of clips

00:00:22.699 --> 00:00:25.340
I recorded of me talking over it,
because I’m gonna be honest,

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.220
it’s one of the faster ways to
make a video.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.220
I started out the

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.240
day making Orin a bagel and
then shoveling the walk even

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.000
though I knew dang well that
it wasn’t gonna stop snowing

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.000
for another 12 hours.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.500
Then it was time for Katherine to take

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.329
over shoveling and I went
upstairs to write a couple of

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:38.629
really important emails and
oh my god is that really what

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:39.629
I look like?

00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:41.539
Then Katherine
came in for some recovery time

00:00:41.539 --> 00:00:44.879
and then it was time for a full hour
of Junk Yard Joust, a game where

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:47.059
you put hot wheels down a track
and they get eliminated if they

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:48.429
land on their back of their side.

00:00:48.429 --> 00:00:49.549
Go ahead and pick which team

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.999
you think will win.

00:00:50.999 --> 00:00:53.170
3 of them will,
because Orin doesn’t like it when

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.589
only one team wins.

00:00:54.589 --> 00:00:57.000
I put the names of the teams in a pinned comment below.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.129
You can reply
with the team that you like.

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:02.319
This is currently Orin’s #1 favorite
way to spend time, cars that get

00:01:02.319 --> 00:01:03.510
eliminated go in this box.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.549
He has
a bunch of very specific rules.

00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:07.479
And then of course we had to
watch some actual Junkyard Joust

00:01:07.479 --> 00:01:08.479
on Youtube.

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:10.049
Which is an amazing
Youtube channel if you haven’t

00:01:10.049 --> 00:01:11.049
seen it.

00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:12.049
It is so fun.

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:13.759
And then after
that he was sad that we weren’t

00:01:13.759 --> 00:01:16.288
going to watch any more Youtube
videos so he decided to have a 

00:01:16.288 --> 00:01:18.130
rest underneath this pillow. 

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.920
I then went for a walk to the
coffee shop to get Katherine a

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.200
latte and listen to the climax of
Jade Legacy which is a really amazing book.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.189
And yes I did cry while walking down
the street.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.189
Also on the way I helped push

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:31.250
a truck out of the snow.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.310
I love a snowy walk.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:34.590
I love a snowy town.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.010
I love it when everything slows
down a little bit and everyone has

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.990
to take care of their stuff and take
care of each other.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:40.990
I especially love

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:43.569
when there is a decaf americano
and a croissant at the end of it.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:45.200
Then I had to start writing this script.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.719
This is a video of me writing the words

00:01:46.719 --> 00:01:49.280
I am saying right now, also not
tremendously flattering.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.280
And then, time for more shoveling.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.579
This time I did my neighbor’s walk because

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.799
he’s out of town and then I had to
tweet about how, because of a

00:01:54.799 --> 00:01:56.889
scheduling mistake we had to
push the date of the Project for

00:01:56.889 --> 00:01:59.829
Awesome back to February 25th
which I know is very inconvenient

00:01:59.829 --> 00:02:00.829
for some people.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:02.969
I’m sorry about this. 
We tried to find some

00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:04.259
other way to fix it but we failed.

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:05.530
But yes I am very excited for the

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.999
Project for Awesome, February 25th.

00:02:07.999 --> 00:02:09.999
Everybody get ready. I also just

00:02:09.999 --> 00:02:13.910
uploaded the amazing recap video that
Maia edited, and it’s on Hankschannel

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.599
and you can watch it and remember
all the fun times that we had.

00:02:16.599 --> 00:02:19.710
Then I wrote some more emails and I wrote a
tweet about how my pants were wet

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.840
because of the truck that sprayed
snow all over me.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.540
Then I recorded a secret video for somebody else that I can’t tell you about right now.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.010
And I also wrote a bunch of other
stuff that I also can’t really tell you

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.010
about right now.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.810
And look, one of the
really fantastic things about vlogbrothers

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.900
is that we often come to an important
point at the end of the video.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.870
But often times, we don’t.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.200
Sometimes life is just about life.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.370
It’s about doing all the things you
wanted to do that day, or you needed

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.370
to do that day.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.709
Sometimes it’s about
2,000 videos of content, 15 years of life

00:02:46.709 --> 00:02:49.769
doing things that I couldn’t imagine
because they didn’t exist.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.769
And always,

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:53.150
always, because a bunch of people
working together to keep each other

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.050
honest and push for really interesting
and useful stuff to exist in the world.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.140
That stuff existed!

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:01.060
And the amazing
thing is, I have no idea if I’m halfway

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:02.159
through this.

00:03:02.159 --> 00:03:04.110
Have I made most of the
videos I will ever make?

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:05.120
I don’t know.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.120
Probably.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.310
1,000 videos is a lot of videos.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.310
But I don’t know.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.310
I’m not looking too hard at it.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:13.510
Because I certainly could not have guessed how the last 15 years would go.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:17.340
What an amazing run! So weird! So much fun!

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.069
And so many amazing things that would
not have been possible without this

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:25.299
community or the people who work
at Complexly and at Vidcon and at DFTBA.

00:03:25.299 --> 00:03:28.020
And finally, the moment you have
been waiting for: here are your

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.239
Junkyard Joust winners.

00:03:29.239 --> 00:03:31.090
Congratulations to the white team,

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.940
the green team, and the batmobiles.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.860
John, thank you and I will

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.920
see you on Tuesday.

